WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.610
A duke lies on a couch
while musicians play.

2
00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:09.500
"If music be the food of love, play on,"
The music notes turn into food on a plate.

3
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.140
Moments later, he pushes it away.

4
00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:15.430
Above him hang two frames, both covered.

5
00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.970
One is labelled Olivia,
the woman he says he loves.

6
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.270
The other, love itself.

7
00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.410
He says he's sick with love.

8
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.800
But who is he really in love with?

9
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:29.920
In this mission, you'll take apart
the very first speech of the play.

10
00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.910
You'll find out why lovesick
sighing was a fashion,

11
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.050
backed by a theory of the body.

12
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.000
And you'll catch Orsino
saying one thing about love,

13
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.390
then the opposite.

14
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.140
Your mission: decide whether
Orsino loves Olivia or love itself.
